**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests`

**How to implement.** Dropping entry files onto the Materials window opens the import dialog over them (001 §H; .spec-md §3.7: a dropped file always opens the dialog; §10.1 discoverability: the dialog opens on a dropped entry file; §10.4: the dialog's completion message updates the window's model, whose projections re-query the store, so no reload is needed; the S3.2 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`. (a) `MaterialsWindowContext` gains `openImportDialog : ImportDecision list -> unit`, documented as opening the import dialog over the rows of dropped entries (the composition root bakes the window; tests record). (b) `MaterialsWindowModel` gains `importStatus : ControlCaption option` and `importError : CatalogueImportError option`, each opening `None`, each with a one-line doc. (c) `MaterialsWindowMsg` gains, each documented, `DropMaterialEntryFiles of FileName list` and `MaterialsImportApplied of summary : ControlCaption`. (d) `updateMaterialsWindow`. `DropMaterialEntryFiles files` calls `context.catalogueImports.decideDroppedFiles files` (step 104). `Ok []` leaves the model as it was. `Ok decisions` calls `context.openImportDialog decisions` and clears `importStatus` and `importError`. `Error e` sets `importError` to `Some e` and clears `importStatus`; no dialog opens. `MaterialsImportApplied summary` sets `importStatus` to `Some summary` and clears `importError`; the next render re-queries the store, so an added material is listed. Neither arms or disarms a gate or changes the mode. (e) The view: after `messageRow` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:messageRow`), when either is set, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `materialsImportStatusText` shows `importError`'s `caption` (step 101) in `messageColor`, or else `importStatus`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs`. The context's `openImportDialog` is `fun decisions -> ImportDialogWindow(catalogueImports, ApplyDroppedEntries decisions, fun applied -> dispatch (MaterialsImportApplied applied.summary)).Show()` (step 108). `member _.DropEntryFiles (files : FileName list) : unit` dispatches `DropMaterialEntryFiles files`: the semantic seam that the drop and the tests share, as `Retarget` is the launcher's. After `Program.run`, `EntryFileDrop.acceptEntryFiles this (fun files -> dispatch (DropMaterialEntryFiles files))` (step 108). The class doc names the drop in no more words. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Materials window group: `materialsImportStatusText` (`"MaterialsImportStatusText"`) under a one-line comment citing spec 0050 S3.2. (4) Tests, in `MaterialsWindowTests`. `stubContext` (step 109) passes a recording `openImportDialog`. Files are written as step 104's facts write them, into a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "MaterialsWindowTests")`. `dropping entry files on the Materials window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing`: `DropMaterialEntryFiles` of a new user material's file records one `openImportDialog` holding one `EntryIdNotHeld` row, `importError` stays `None`, and the context's import seam does not hold the material. `a refused drop on the Materials window shows its reason and opens no dialog`: `DropMaterialEntryFiles [ notes.txt ]` sets `importError` to `Some (DroppedFileRefusedErr _)` and records no dialog. `an applied import of dropped files is the Materials window status`: `MaterialsImportApplied` of a summary sets `importStatus` to it and clears `importError`. `the Materials window accepts dropped files`: a `MaterialsWindow` mounted as the class mounts one answers `DragDrop.GetAllowDrop` true. `acceptance: a material file dropped on the Materials window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library` (trait `ui-smoke`): over `AppContext.create (TestAppScope.fileLocations …)`, a `MaterialsWindow(ctx.materials, ctx.categories, ctx.catalogueImports)` is shown headless. After `window.DropEntryFiles` of a new user material's file, exactly one `ImportDialogWindow` opens, observed through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent` as `LauncherTests.clickAndObserve` observes. Pressing its `importApplyButton` closes it, `ctx.materials.tryGetMaterial` resolves the material, and `materialsImportStatusText` shows the summary.

**Acceptance.** After the drop is wired, a file dropped on the Materials window MUST be decided through `decideDroppedFiles` and open `ImportDialogWindow`, applying nothing before Apply; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a material file dropped on the Materials window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `dropping entry files on the Materials window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing`, `a refused drop on the Materials window shows its reason and opens no dialog`, `an applied import of dropped files is the Materials window status`, `the Materials window accepts dropped files`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.
